traints\n\n- The number of nodes in the list is in the range `[0, 5000]`.\n- `-5000 <= Node.val <= 5000`\n","hidden":false,"slug":"reverse-linked-list","solved":0,"createdAt":"2026-06-11T16:23:55.698Z","updatedAt":"2026-06-11T19:25:36.959Z","difficulty":"EASY","defaultCode":[{"id":"cmq9pjaai0006xexavzcvpzyz","languageId":5,"problemId":"cmq9pj9kk0000xexa57k5wvyn","code":"/*\n * Definition for singly-linked list.\n * public class ListNode {\n *     int val;\n *     ListNode next;\n *     ListNode(int x) { val = x; }\n * }\n */\n\nimport java.util.*;\n\nclass Solution {\n    public ListNode solve(ListNode head) {\n        \n    }\n}\n","createdAt":"2026-06-11T16:23:56.634Z","updatedAt":"2026-06-11T19:25:37.432Z"},{"id":"cmq9pj9u00002xexal5noq68o","languageId":2,"problemId":"cmq9pj9kk0000xexa57k5wvyn","code":"// Definition for singly-linked list.\n// struct ListNode {\n//     int val;\n//     ListNode *next;\n//     ListNode(int x) : val(x), next(nullptr) {}\n// };\n\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\n\nclass Solution {\npublic:\n    ListNode* solve(ListNode* head) {\n        \n    }\n};\n","createdAt":"2026-06-11T16:23:56.040Z","updatedAt":"2026-06-11T19:25:37.120Z"},{"id":"cmq9pja4o0004xexagqs1c5ou","languageId":4,"problemId":"cmq9pj9kk0000xexa57k5wvyn","code":"// Definition for singly-linked list.\n// struct ListNode {\n//     int val;\n//     ListNode *next;\n//     ListNode(int x) : val(x), next(nullptr) {}\n// };\n\n#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n#include <string.h>\n#include <stdbool.h>\n\nListNode* solve(ListNode* head) {\n    \n}\n","createdAt":"2026-06-11T16:23:56.424Z","updatedAt":"2026-06-11T19:25:37.275Z"},{"id":"cmq9pjafo0008xexa7phyxgc9","languageId":6,"problemId":"cmq9pj9kk0000xexa57k5wvyn","code":"# Definition for singly-linked list.\n# class ListNode:\n#     def __init__(self, val=0, next=None):\n#         self.val = val\n#         self.next = next\n\nclass Solution:\n    def solve(self, head: Optional[ListNode]) -> Optional[Lis