Z","updatedAt":"2026-06-11T19:25:38.059Z"},{"id":"cmq9pjazo000fxexadprcktk8","languageId":4,"problemId":"cmq9pjar2000bxexarmhh7awo","code":"// Definition for a binary tree node.\n// struct TreeNode {\n//     int val;\n//     TreeNode *left;\n//     TreeNode *right;\n//     TreeNode(int x) : val(x), left(nullptr), right(nullptr) {}\n// };\n\n#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n#include <string.h>\n#include <stdbool.h>\n\nint solve(TreeNode* root) {\n    \n}\n","createdAt":"2026-06-11T16:23:57.540Z","updatedAt":"2026-06-11T19:25:38.215Z"},{"id":"cmq9pjb4s000hxexaethxr4f1","languageId":5,"problemId":"cmq9pjar2000bxexarmhh7awo","code":"/*\n * Definition for a binary tree node.\n * public class TreeNode {\n *     int val;\n *     TreeNode left;\n *     TreeNode right;\n *     TreeNode(int x) { val = x; }\n * }\n */\n\nimport java.util.*;\n\nclass Solution {\n    public int solve(TreeNode root) {\n        \n    }\n}\n","createdAt":"2026-06-11T16:23:57.724Z","updatedAt":"2026-06-11T19:25:38.389Z"},{"id":"cmq9pjb9o000jxexawzfk2inv","languageId":6,"problemId":"cmq9pjar2000bxexarmhh7awo","code":"# Definition for a binary tree node.\n# class TreeNode:\n#     def __init__(self, val=0, left=None, right=None):\n#         self.val = val\n#         self.left = left\n#         self.right = right\n\nclass Solution:\n    def solve(self, root: Optional[TreeNode]) -> int:\n        pass\n","createdAt":"2026-06-11T16:23:57.900Z","updatedAt":"2026-06-11T19:25:38.547Z"},{"id":"cmq9pjbgp000lxexaq2mnmts7","languageId":7,"problemId":"cmq9pjar2000bxexarmhh7awo","code":"// Definition for a binary tree node.\n// type TreeNode struct {\n//     Val int\n//     Left *TreeNode\n//     Right *TreeNode\n// }\n\npackage main\n\nimport (\n    \"fmt\"\n    \"math\"\n)\n\nfunc solve(root *TreeNode) int {\n    \n}\n","createdAt":"2026-06-11T16:23:58.153Z","updatedAt":"2026-06-11T19:25:38.701Z"}]},{"id":"cmq9pjckf000xxexa8ohc5ils","title":"Find if Path Exists in Graph","description":"## Find if Path Exists in Graph\n\nThere is a bi-directional graph with `n` vertices, where each vertex is labeled from `0` to `n-1`. The edges in the graph are represented as a 2D integer array `edges`, where each `edges[i] = [u, v]` denotes a bi-directional edge between vertex `u` and vertex `v`.\n\nGiven two integers `source` and `destination`, return `true` if there is a valid path from `source` to `destination`, or `false` otherwise.\n\nInput format: first line is `n` (vertices) and `m` (edges), next `m` lines each contain two space-separated integers `u v`, last line contains `source` and `destination`.\n\n#### Example 1\n\nInput\n\n```\n3 2\n0 1\n1 2\n0 2\n```\n\nOutput\n\n```\ntrue\n```\n\n#### Example 2\n\nInput\n\n```\n6 4\n0 1\n0 2\n3 5\n5 4\n0 5\n```\n\nOutput\n\n```\nfalse\n```\n\n#### Example 3\n\nInput\n\n```\n1 0\n0 0\n```\n\nOutput\n\n```\ntrue\n```\n\n#### Constraints\n\n- `1 <= n <= 2 * 10^5`\n- `0 <= m <= 2 * 10^5`\n- `0 <= u, v < n`\n- `u != v` (no self-loops)\n- `0 <= source, destination < n`\n","hidden":false,"slug":"find-if-path-exists-in-graph","solved":0,"createdAt":"2026-06-11T16:23:59.584Z","updatedAt":"2026-06-11T19:25:39.785Z","difficulty":"EASY","defaultCode":[{"id":"cmq9pjcos000zxexar71qxkvd","languageId":2,"problemId":"cmq9pjckf000xxexa8ohc5ils","code":"#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\n\nclass Solution {\npublic:\n    bool solve(int n, vector<vector<int>>& edges, int source, int destination) {\n        \n    }\n};\n","createdAt":"2026-06-11T16:23:59.741Z","updatedAt":"2026-06-11T19:25:39.942Z"},{"id":"cmq9pjcvu0011xexaz4pd3unk","languageId":4,"problemId":"cmq9pjckf000xxexa8ohc5ils","code":"#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n#include <string.h>\n#include <stdbool.h>\n\nbool solve(int n, int** edges, int edgesSize, int* edgesColSize, int source, int destination) {\n    \n}\n","createdAt":"2026-06-11T16:23:59.995Z","updatedAt":"2026-06-11T19:25:40.103Z"},{"id":"cmq9pjd1h0013xexacsft8roi","languageId":5,"problemId":"cmq9pjckf000xxexa8o